class:: ShaderBuffer
summary:: Float32 GPU-data resource for the SCShader spectrum binding
categories:: External>Graphics
related:: Guides/SCShader, Classes/Shader, Classes/ShaderFFTTexture, Classes/ShaderWaveformTexture

description::
ShaderBuffer owns a finite Float32 array in the language and a matching one-row code::R32Float:: GPU texture in the renderer. code::setn:: sends values as big-endian float32 OSC blobs in chunks of at most 2048 values, keeping each packet below the usual macOS UDP datagram ceiling. The renderer uploads the complete padded texture after each accepted chunk. The v1 limit is 16384 values, additionally restricted by the GPU's maximum one-row texture width; unsupported lengths report an error without terminating the renderer.

Bind it using code::shader.setBuffer(\spectrum, buffer)::. link::Classes/ShaderFFTTexture:: and link::Classes/ShaderWaveformTexture:: bind their owned buffers automatically. In WGSL the fixed binding is code::@group(0) @binding(3) var spectrum_buffer: texture_2d<f32>::. It is non-filterable, so use code::textureLoad(spectrum_buffer, vec2<i32>(bin, 0), 0).r::. This is not general WGSL reflection, arbitrary storage buffers, shared-memory transport, or a replacement for link::Classes/Buffer::.

classmethods::

method:: float

argument:: length
Number of Float32 values from 1 through 16384.

argument:: server
Ready ShaderServer. Defaults to code::ShaderServer.default::.

method:: new

argument:: length
Number of Float32 values from 1 through 16384.

argument:: server
Ready ShaderServer. Defaults to code::ShaderServer.default::.

instancemethods::

method:: set

argument:: index
Zero-based Float32 index.

argument:: value
Finite numeric value.

method:: setn

argument:: start
Zero-based first index. Defaults to 0.

argument:: array
Finite numeric values for consecutive indices.

method:: value

argument:: index
Zero-based index.

returns::
The current language-side Float32 value.

method:: asArray

returns::
A copy of the language-side Float32 values. This is useful for inspection and tests; it does not read back from the GPU.

method:: free

discussion::
Releases the renderer resource. A Shader whose active spectrum buffer is freed falls back to an internal zero-filled one-row texture.

examples::

This example uses the packaged extension. Run one demo at a time and wait for setup to finish. It creates its own resources; no earlier example is required. See link::Guides/SCShader:: for the full walkthrough.

code::
(
var source = ShaderDef.filenameSymbol.asString.dirname.dirname +/+ "shaders/fullscreen.wgsl";
v = ShaderServer.new(\bufferHelp);
v.waitForBoot { |server|
    d = ShaderDef(\helpPulse, source);
    x = Shader(d, [\amount, 0.5], server);
    b = ShaderBuffer.float(128, server);
    b.setn(0, Array.fill(128, { |index| index / 127 }));
    x.setBuffer(\spectrum, b);
};
)
::

Cleanup before starting another example; wait for any renderer window to close:

code::
(
b.free; x.free; d.free; v.free;
)
::

